          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸೂಜಿ (sūji) — \"a needle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸೂಜಿ (sūji) is what the ನೂಲು (nūlu) is put through. It is a borrowing from the north, and it arrived early enough that nothing about it feels foreign now."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is also the hand of a clock. A ಗಂಟೆ has two ಸೂಜಿ (sūji) on its face, and Kannada saw the resemblance before anybody thought to give the hands a separate name."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two."
            }
          ]
        },
