              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪೊರಕೆ (porake) — \"a broom\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪೊರಕೆ (porake) is a bundle of stiff ribs tied at one end — no handle, so it is used bent over, in short strokes."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is the first object of the day. The ground outside the ಬಾಗಿಲು is swept with a ಪೊರಕೆ (porake) before the ರಂಗೋಲಿ is set out on it, because the pattern needs clean ground to sit on. Sweeping, then drawing: that order is fixed."
            }
          ]
        },
